zornyX3D Studio v2019BeTA+ 1.2.6.6 forms the foundation stone of the development journey as the first version in the history of this original game engine. Due to the passage of time, deleted digital archives, formatted old disks, and the years that have passed, the source code and original files of this first prototype have unfortunately been completely lost, blending into the dusty shelves of history. All that remains are the memories of this early period in memory and old development logs.  
What Was Built in This First Version?
Raw Python and Ursina Foundations: Instead of complex libraries, the first version offered a revolutionary yet primitive single-file (zornyx3d_studio.py) IDE architecture using the rawest and simplest form of Python 3 and the Ursina engine.  
Original English Scripting Language: The first parser was written in this version, allowing developers to create and move 3D objects using entirely minimalist English commands like SPAWN, SCALE, ON_KEY, and COLLIDER without needing to know Python.  
Basic 3D Prototyping and Mazes: Instead of large games, the first version mostly tested simple 3D cubes, primitive floors, mazes surrounded by blue walls, and red player cubes moving left and right with keyboard keys (W, A, S, D).  
Primitive Debug Console: Red, semi-transparent error panels overlaying the screen upon the slightest syntax error while writing or running code were first introduced to developers in this version.  
Even though its code and files were lost over time, zornyX3D Studio v2019BeTA+ 1.2.6.6 will always be the most special beginning of this adventure as the birthplace of the engine, where its code-driven philosophy was established, and the first gateway to the retro 3D world.  
